; The west end: Netty's cottage with the washing out, her nets, and the landing stage where Maud
; comes to feed the gulls.
prop oak 3 4
prop cottage-teal 3.5 12
entrance netty-cottage 4.125 12.5 to=cottage-b name="A Cottage"
prop washing-line 0.9 13.4
prop barrel-water 6.8 13.1
prop net-rack 9.5 14.4
prop cargo-crate 5 15.5
prop cargo-crate 6.4 15.2
prop cargo-barrel 7.5 16
npc netty 10 15.4 cast=netty facing=down say="Mind the hooks, love.|Nets, nets, nets. My fingers dream in knots.|The Red Gulls took my best net last spring. Wore it as a cape."
npc maud 6 21 cast=maud facing=down say="He loved the gulls, my Edric.|By the posts. It's somewhere by the posts.|Thirty years of bells, and now it's so quiet."
npc harbour-brat 8 16.4 look=523 name="A Harbour Brat" wander=3 say="Bet I can spit further than you!|The Red Gulls took my cap. Then my brother's cap.|Gulls are just rats that went to sea."

; The west warehouse, a porter, and the cook off the Gull's Wager buying for the next voyage.
prop warehouse 11.5 12
entrance warehouse-west 11.8125 12.5 to=warehouse name="A Warehouse"
prop sack-pile 9 13.1
prop crate-stack 14.4 13.1
prop barrel-salt 15.7 13.4
npc porter 13.4 14.2 look=553 name="A Porter" facing=left say="Mind your toes, coming through.|Warehouse is full. Warehouse is always full.|They pay by the crate, not the hour. So, quick."
npc ships-cook 15.2 15.6 look=432 name="The Ship's Cook" facing=right say="Off the Gull's Wager? Then you've had my stew. Sorry.|Buying salt pork. Two weeks of it. Pray for us.|Captain Marsh says hello. Actually she says hurry up."

; The Rusty Anvil, Brannock's bar, dim even by day. Nobody goes in yet. Then the pie seller and the
; cart, just short of the trouble.
prop rusty-anvil-plum 19.5 12
prop lamp-arm 17.3 13.2
prop handcart 23.6 13.2
npc pie-seller 22.6 13.8 look=443 name="A Pie Seller" facing=down say="Hot pies! Fish, eel, or mystery!|Mystery's the popular one.|Keep it away from the gulls. They're organised."

; The fishmonger's, where the Red Gulls are shaking down Old Tomas, with the fish stall next door and
; the fishwives watching. A1-C1-01 starts when you walk up to them, with a red ! over them till then.
; There's a way round behind the fishmonger's, so the second trigger, with no mark, catches anyone who
; goes that way. The two never touch, so they can't both go off at once.
prop cherry-tree 27.5 3
prop fishmonger-pink 27.5 12
prop crate-open 26.2 12.9
prop crate-open 29.6 12.9
trigger red-gulls 26 9 w=6 h=9 talk=a1-c1-01 mark=yes when=arrived unless=red-gulls-beaten
trigger red-gulls-behind 27 0 w=2 h=9 talk=a1-c1-01 when=arrived unless=red-gulls-beaten
npc tomas 28.5 15.5 cast=tomas facing=left say="Forty years on this harbour. Never paid a dock tax yet."
npc gull-1 27 15.8 cast=red-gull facing=right unless=red-gulls-beaten
npc gull-2 27.2 14.6 cast=red-gull facing=right unless=red-gulls-beaten
npc gull-3 30 14.6 cast=red-gull facing=left unless=red-gulls-beaten
npc grell 30.6 16.2 cast=grell facing=left unless=grell-gone
npc hale 26 13.4 cast=hale facing=left when=grell-gone say="Lantern Market's up the street and past the fountain. The board's by the inn.|Good work today. Don't make me regret saying it.|Greywatch. Don't ask."
npc watch-1 27.6 12.8 cast=watch facing=down when=grell-gone say="Captain's orders. Keep it moving.|Red Gulls in the water. Best morning in months."
npc watch-2 25 13.6 cast=watch facing=down when=grell-gone say="Red Gulls. Every week it's the Red Gulls.|Not this week, though. Thanks to you."

; The fish stall, the fishwives at it, and the gutter.
prop fish-stall 32 13.7
prop barrel-salt 36.2 14.3
prop crate-open 34.4 17.1
npc fishmonger-a 32.4 14.6 look=104 name="A Fishwife" facing=right say="Herring! Mackerel! Eels as long as your leg!|Fresh this morning. Well. This week.|The Red Gulls never paid for a fish in their lives.|Don't poke the eels. They poke back."
npc fishmonger-b 34.4 14.6 look=236 name="A Fishmonger" facing=left say="Crab, live crab, very angry crab!|Two for a copper, and I'll throw in the smell.|Hale's lot used to walk the boardwalk. Not lately."
npc gutter 36 15.8 look=545 name="A Fish Gutter" facing=left say="Gut, scale, slap it on the board.|Mind your boots. The fish don't.|Tomas brings the best catch. Don't tell him I said."

; The middle warehouse, its cargo, and the hands moving it.
prop warehouse-teal 39.5 12
entrance warehouse-middle 39.8125 12.5 to=warehouse name="A Warehouse"
prop crate-stack 36.6 13.1
prop cargo-crate 42.4 13.2
prop cargo-barrel 43.6 13.4
prop sack-pile 40.6 17.1
npc dock-hand 41.2 14.4 name="A Dock Hand" sheet=farmhand facing=down wander=3 say="Mind the ropes. They bite.|Ship in, ship out. The sea never stops.|Saw you two sort the Red Gulls. Nicely done."
npc gull-victim 38 16 look=416 name="A Gull-Robbed Traveller" wander=3 say="A gull took my pie. My whole pie.|It looked me in the eye while it did it.|I'm going home. Your harbour is lawless.|Don't feed them. They remember faces."

; A townhouse, the ropemaker at the rope posts, and the carrier going back and forth.
prop townhouse-pink 46.5 12
prop barrel-flowers 45.3 13.1
prop lamp-double 48.9 13.3
npc ropemaker 46.4 16.3 look=402 name="The Ropemaker" facing=down say="Good rope's the only thing that holds in this town.|Mind the coil. It's longer than it looks.|A sailor's best friend. After the bottle."
npc carrier 50 15.2 name="A Carrier" sheet=porter facing=left wander=4 say="Another ship, another hundred crates.|My back is a rumour. I carry crates on it anyway.|Don't stand there. Stand anywhere else."

; The chandler's, and a sailor stocking up.
prop house-shop 54.5 12
entrance chandler 56.44 12.5 to=shop name="The Chandler's"
prop sacks 51.6 13.3
prop cargo-barrel 59.4 13.2
prop net-rack 54.6 17.3
npc sailor-e 53 14.8 look=615 name="A Sailor" facing=up say="Rope, tar, biscuit, and something for my nerves.|The chandler's prices would make a pirate blush.|Off on the evening tide. Wish me a dull voyage."

; The Watch's post at the foot of the road, the customs clerk, the harbourmaster with the book, and
; the sailors in off the east jetty.
prop watch-post 63.5 12
prop chalkboard 68.2 13.3
prop crate-stack 61.2 13.3
npc customs-clerk 67 13.6 look=447 name="A Customs Clerk" facing=left say="Cargo? Declare it. Contraband? Also declare it.|The harbourmaster's book is full. So is mine.|Every crate's a story. Most of them are lies."
npc harbourmaster 64 15.4 name="The Harbourmaster" sheet=traveller facing=left say="Names go in the book. Not today, mind. The book's full.|Ships from the east come in grey with ash. Odd times.|Captain Marsh is the only captain who docks on time."
npc sailor-c 60.4 18.6 look=196 name="A Sailor" facing=right say="Back from the east. Never again, I said. Said it twice.|The sky over the Strait's gone the colour of old porridge.|Shore leave at last. I could kiss these planks."
npc sailor-d 61.8 19.2 look=111 name="A Sailor" facing=left say="Don't whistle on the dock. Bad luck.|Lost a hat to a gull this morning. Good hat.|They say Greywatch eats soldiers. Rumours, mind."
npc bosun 61 22 look=616 name="A Bosun" facing=down say="Lines fore and aft, and smartly!|Never trust a calm harbour.|Lost three hands to the city last night. They'll be back when the coin runs out."

